  "id": "cape_malay_choir_nederlandslied",
  "name": "Cape Malay choirs (nederlandslied and moppie)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Competition choirs of Cape Town's Muslim community, the Malay choirs or nagtroepe, which compete each year under bodies such as the Cape Malay Choir Board in categories including the nederlandslied and the moppie. The nederlandslied, a song in Dutch or Afrikaans descended from old Dutch repertoire, sets a solo voice with dense melismatic ornament against the choir, while the moppie is a fast comic song. The choirs are accompanied by a string band of guitars, banjos and bass, with the ghoema drum in the comic songs. The banjo card stands in for the banjos and the hand-drum card for the ghoema.",
